      { "text": "Uptake into presynaptic vesicles where the active product is stored and released", "explanation": "Correct. Methyldopa is cleared from plasma rapidly, which gives the short 1.5 to 2 hour half-life, but it is taken up into presynaptic vesicles and converted there to alpha-methylnorepinephrine. That product is stored in the vesicle and released as a false transmitter over a long period, so the pharmacodynamic effect lasts 24 to 48 hours even though the parent drug is long gone. The site of action, not the plasma concentration, sets the duration, which is why it is still dosed two to three times daily for tolerability." }
