      { "text": "Coronary vasospasm from unopposed alpha-mediated constriction of the epicardial arteries", "explanation": "Incorrect. Nothing in this regimen blocks beta receptors or leaves alpha-mediated coronary constriction unopposed, and the mechanism described is not a feature of potassium channel openers. This would be the correct answer if a nonselective beta blocker had been given to a patient with vasospastic angina." }
